+# Agent Note: Immutable tool capabilities
+
+Status: implemented
+
+English | [中文](2026-10-04-immutable-tool-capabilities.zh.md)
+
+## Problem
+
+Name-based policy loses delegation classification through aliases and nested dispatch. Mutable definitions and around-dispatch listeners can change the execution identity after admission. PTC dispatch logging can begin before admission rejects the descendant.
+
+## Decision
+
+The registry captures capability and required descendant metadata at registration, retains registered-body provenance for aliases, and publishes an immutable execution capability union. Each nested dispatch validates its live parent token and exact Agent identity; asynchronous execution carries its parent independently of caller arguments. Monotonic guards check before policy, after admission, before wrappers and immediately before the body. PTC admits the actual descendant before logging dispatch facts; its catalog does not give harmless inspection the delegation classification.
+
+The [cooperative cancellation decision](2026-07-19-cooperative-tool-cancellation.md) remains active: wrappers can replace only the cancellation signal. This decision extends immutable execution identity without replacing cancellation ownership.
+
+Omitted or empty classification contributes `unclassified`, and an explicitly required descendant with unknown classification denies admission. The registry alone labels its PTC transport `nested-dispatch`; policy exempts that transport while checking actual descendants, and any read/control exemption requires every union key to belong to its explicit allowed classes.
+
+Independent Agent drivers start a new root tool context through the host-only `withAgentDriver` operation, which validates the exact live Agent generation before leaving the enclosing tool context. The caller's context is restored after scheduling; ordinary nested calls retain parent validation and capability checks. This preserves child-to-parent relay without accepting cross-Agent nested tokens.
+
+## Alternatives considered
+
+**Name-only denial.** Aliases and composites change names while retaining the delegated effect.
+
+**Classify the entire PTC catalog.** A harmless inspection would inherit unrelated delegation capabilities and become unavailable.
+
+## Verification
+
+The focused registry/executor and shipped Consumer tests reject direct, aliased, declared composite and dynamic nested delegation before Consumer/provider/log effects, preserve asynchronous parent identity, and reject missing references, cycles and expired parent tokens. Mutation and disposal cannot weaken captured classification. Disabled Team policy leaves admitted tools compatible.
+
+## Consequences
+
+Required descendant references are resolved in the current Agent view and deny when a dependency is disposed or restricted. Capability metadata is host-owned and does not sandbox arbitrary same-process plugin code.
