+# Agent Note: Reserved continuable admission and prompt preparation
+
+Status: implemented
+
+English | [中文](2026-10-04-reserved-continuable-admission.zh.md)
+
+## Problem
+
+Attachment owners require the exact child scope before execution. Materialization that immediately submits input cannot guarantee this ordering, and ordinary cold resume can bypass the owner after restart. Request retries also need current scoped contributions and authorization after asynchronous route preparation.
+
+## Decision
+
+The host separates creation, durable initial persistence and execution release. The owner-only AgentHandle capability gates every wake. Durable reservation and initial-admission events retain child identity, idempotency, release and cancellation. Owner recovery closes execution even for activated records; a claimed initial item without committed user admission is restored under the same message id. Consumed input stays deduplicated. Legacy starts explicitly permit automatic recovery.
+
+Prompt preparation is awaited and scoped before every attempt assembly. Retries reassemble sections, context and tools without repeating pre-step interception or accepted user admission. Model-visible changes use existing logged channels. Final model admission follows asynchronous route preparation, so authority revocation cannot be missed during those awaits.
+
+## Alternatives considered
+
+A binder callback inside subagent creation couples host execution to one domain and exposes unrestricted orchestration. An ordinary durable inbox insertion without an owner gate permits direct wakes and restart to run too early. Reusing a rendered retry assembly preserves stale owner contributions. These choices do not satisfy owner installation and revocation ordering.
+
+## Consequences
+
+The standard factory declares deferred-execution support before reserved creation. Explicit reservations reject generic resume and ordinary continuation delivery. Tombstones precede disposal; deadline cutoff returns while late cleanup stays observed and execution remains closed. Focused tests independently observe durable quarantine, idempotency, activation and restart, direct wake denial, refreshed retry history, and provider denial on refresh failure or revoked authorization.
+
+Asynchronous admission listeners can revoke authority after an earlier listener approved it. Synchronous exact-generation execution guards therefore follow the complete asynchronous chain and run immediately before provider dispatch or deferred execution release. This also covers revocation during activation flush. Runtime disposal retains one shared cleanup result so later calls cannot hide the first failure; malformed durable admission values fail through the stable state error.
