+# Agent Note: Active catalog replacement declarations
+
+Status: implemented
+
+English | [中文](2026-10-04-active-catalog-replacements.zh.md)
+
+## Problem
+
+The installation retains original prototype source while build entry projects select replacement GAT packages. Whole-source catalog discovery sees duplicate event, service and client declarations, so it cannot regenerate required admission events safely.
+
+## Decision
+
+Catalog source discovery retains its exhaustive glob corpus. It excludes one retained prototype only when an entry project explicitly excludes that package and references its replacement. Discovery validates the replacement project and fails on incomplete configuration. Existing workspaces without replacements retain the complete corpus. Persistence, Cordis and client-slot generators share the same selection. Generated artifacts remain generator-owned.
+
+## Alternatives considered
+
+Deleting prototype files can discard existing work. Hand-editing generated vocabulary hides freshness failures. Filtering every package absent from the build graph can hide newly added unregistered contracts. Explicit paired replacement selection preserves exhaustive detection elsewhere.
+
+## Consequences
+
+Catalog generators reflect the selected package declarations while retained files remain reviewable. Fixtures must prove unchanged default discovery, valid exclusions, incomplete configuration rejection, and unrelated-source visibility. The selection changes documentation generation only; it grants no runtime authority or deployment approval.
+
+## Testing
+
+[Catalog discovery tests](../../../../scripts/catalog-source-files.spec.ts) verify exhaustive default discovery, each declared replacement exclusion, independent replacement validation for narrow caller corpora, and rejection of missing or contradictory replacements. The affected catalog freshness checks verify generated artifacts against the selected declarations.
+
+## Risks
+
+A future replacement must add an explicit ownership pair and regression fixture. An incorrect build selection can halt generation; that failure preserves original declarations and requires correcting the selection.
