+## Prompt preparation and reserved execution
+
+`agent/prepare-prompt` is an awaited serial event scoped to the exact Agent with turn, step, attempt and signal. It runs before assembly for the first attempt and retries. Retry reassembly refreshes contributions without repeating pre-step interception or user admission. Rendered text is logged by system-message reconciliation. Creation and resume can defer execution; only the returned handle exposes release. The durable `agent/execution-reserved` event distinguishes explicit and automatic recovery. Generic resume denies explicit reservations unless their owner requests deferred reconstruction.
+
+The final serial `agent/model-admission` event revalidates exact owner authority after route preparation and before user/system admission and provider dispatch. `AgentFactory.supportsDeferredExecution` prevents an incapable factory from materializing an ungated reserved child.
+
+`agents.guardExecution(agent, guard)` registers a synchronous, exact-generation policy through the calling scope effect. Guards return `undefined` and may throw to deny; asynchronous callbacks are excluded by the public type. Final model checks run after every asynchronous model-admission listener and again immediately before provider streaming. Deferred handle release applies the same guards with activation kind. Disposing the registration removes that exact callback; owners close execution before relinquishing required policies.
