+## Reserved continuable children
+
+A `ReservedContinuable` exposes exact child Agent/scope, state, persist, activate, abort and dispose operations. States are materialized, inbox-persisted, activated, aborted and disposed. Versioned `subagent/initial-admission` events retain quarantined initial content, identity and idempotency, then activated or aborted edges. Same key/content returns the original id; mismatches fail. Operations share the child serializer. Persistence flush precedes success; abort flushes its tombstone before disposal. Recovery validates the child-owned descriptor and parent, closes execution before publication and installs no owner contributions itself. Activation never duplicates a released or consumed message. Legacy recovery is limited to automatic reservations.
+
+Creation failure remains the primary error when rollback also fails; rollback failures are logged after disposal is attempted. Abort and dispose synchronously close execution, then serialize physical cleanup. Abort persists its tombstone before releasing the generation; cancellation can bound the caller wait while the observed cleanup continues.
+
+Owner recovery restores the original initial message id when a released item was claimed before user admission committed. A consumed initial message is never reinserted. Owner cutoff closes execution synchronously; deadline cancellation returns promptly while tombstone persistence and teardown remain observed.
+
+Durable initial-admission payloads reject non-record values with `CONTINUABLE_STATE_CONFLICT`. Runtime disposal owns one memoized cleanup promise: repeated and concurrent calls retain its success or failure, while caller deadlines only bound that caller wait. Activation applies exact-generation synchronous execution guards after the durable flush and immediately before the execution gate opens.
