+<a id="reserved-admission-and-request-preparation"></a>
+## Reserved admission and request preparation
+
+Deferred agents retain queued input without driving until their owner releases execution. Every request attempt, including retries, awaits scoped `agent/prepare-prompt` and assembles current contributions. Refreshed system text and runtime context are reconciled into durable history before dispatch. Final `agent/model-admission` authorization follows asynchronous route preparation, before input commit and provider dispatch.
+
+The loop applies synchronous execution guards after all asynchronous admission listeners, before input commit and immediately before provider streaming. Deferred handle release applies activation guards immediately before waking its driver.
+
+The TypeScript `request-refresh` and Python `sdk-request-refresh` recorded scenarios exercise assembled system-message history through the public SDK clients. Both use an [awaited fixture contribution](../../../scripts/fixtures/sdk-request-refresh.mjs); request histories and SDK notifications expose refreshed text. [Focused loop tests](tests/prepare-prompt.spec.ts) own retry and denial checks.
