+<a id="reserved-admission-and-request-preparation"></a>
+## Reserved admission and request preparation
+
+The standard adjacent sender keeps its internal symbol marker through registry snapshots, so legacy continuation prompts retain parent-return guidance and the actual relay route.
+
+
+`materializeContinuable()` returns a reserved child with its exact Agent and scope. `persistInitialPrompt()` flushes one quarantined initial item and idempotency record without wake. `activate()` durably releases that item and opens execution. `recoverContinuable()` reconstructs with execution closed, even for an activated record, and restores the same initial message if a first attempt claimed it without committing user admission. Ordinary delivery cannot release explicit reservations. Abort writes a tombstone before teardown; a cleanup deadline closes admission immediately while late cleanup remains observed. The legacy `startContinuable()` wrapper uses these stages with automatic recovery.
+
+Activation revalidates synchronous owner execution guards after flushing durable state and immediately before wake. Repeated and concurrent disposal share the original cleanup result, including rejection; an optional deadline bounds only the caller wait.
+
